  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Two Loaders, One Runtime",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Resolution, Defined",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Resolution = specifier string turned into an absolute path.",
            "'fs' becomes a built-in, no disk touched.",
            "'./util.js' becomes /app/src/util.js.",
            "'lodash/merge' becomes .../node_modules/lodash/merge.js."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Loaders Ship Together"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Loader",
            "Syntax",
            "Age"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CommonJS",
              "require / module.exports",
              "2009"
            ],
            [
              "ESM",
              "import / export",
              "ES2015 spec"
            ],
            [
              "ESM in Node",
              "stable",
              "Node 12+"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sync vs Three Phases"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CJS: require() blocks, returns the value at once.",
            "require() can sit anywhere — inside an if, inside a loop.",
            "ESM phases: construction, instantiation, evaluation.",
            "Construction parses and resolves every specifier first.",
            "So imports hoist and are statically analysable."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "import x from './a.js'   // static only",
            "const n = './b.js'",
            "// import y from n       // SyntaxError",
            "const y = await import(n) // Promise, runtime ok"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Snapshot vs Live Binding"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CJS exports a value snapshot of module.exports.",
            "ESM exports live bindings into every importer.",
            "Reassign `let count` inside the module — importers see the new value."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "export let count = 0",
            "export const bump = () => { count++ }",
            "// importer reads 1 after bump()",
            "// CJS twin would still read 0"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Specifiers Are URLs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "ESM resolution produces a `file:` URL, not a plain path.",
            "So `%20` is decoded to a space before the stat().",
            "`?query` and `#hash` suffixes survive into the cache key.",
            "'./a.js?v=2' is a second, separate module instance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Builtins Win First"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "'fs', 'path' resolve before any filesystem probe.",
            "`node:fs` is unambiguous — cannot be shadowed by node_modules.",
            "A package literally named `fs` can hijack the bare form."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "text": "CJS resolution = filesystem probing with extension guessing. ESM resolution = strict URL resolution, no guessing, with package.json fields as the only escape hatch. Everything past this page is the detail of those two algorithms."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Two Loaders, One Runtime (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "require(X) Has Five Branches"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "X looks like",
            "Branch"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "'fs', 'node:fs'",
              "core, return builtin"
            ],
            [
              "'./ ../ /'",
              "relative to dirname(Y)"
            ],
            [
              "'#alias'",
              "package `imports` field"
            ],
            [
              "'lodash'",
              "node_modules walk"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Node docs name it `require(X) from module at path Y`.",
            "Memorise the branch order — it explains every surprise later.",
            "Relative branch runs LOAD_AS_FILE, then LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "LOAD_AS_FILE Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attempt",
            "Note"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "X",
              "exact name, any extension"
            ],
            [
              "X.js",
              "the common hit"
            ],
            [
              "X.json",
              "parsed, not executed"
            ],
            [
              "X.node",
              "compiled C++ addon"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "First hit wins; later candidates never stat().",
            "This guessing is why `require('./util')` works.",
            "ESM deliberately dropped the whole convenience."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read X/package.json; if `main` exists, resolve it as a file.",
            "Extension guessing applies to the `main` value too.",
            "No package.json: try X/index.js, X/index.json, X/index.node."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "File Beats Directory"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "./util.js        <- wins",
            "./util/index.js  <- ignored",
            "# LOAD_AS_FILE runs before LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Debugging Primitive"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "require.resolve('lodash')   // path, no load",
            "require.resolve('./util')   // proves the guess",
            "require.resolve('x', { paths: ['/other'] })"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`resolve` runs the full algorithm but never executes the file.",
            "`paths` overrides the search roots — resolve as if from elsewhere."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "CJS Probing And The node_modules Walk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "require(esm) Is Now Legal"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Node 22: behind `--experimental-require-module`.",
            "Node 23+: on by default.",
            "Works when the graph is synchronous; returns the namespace object."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "NODE_MODULES_PATHS(Y)"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "/app/src/a.js",
              "/app/src/node_modules",
              "/app/node_modules",
              "/node_modules"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every ancestor dir plus '/node_modules', deepest first.",
            "Dirs already named node_modules are skipped when building the list.",
            "So there is never a /app/node_modules/node_modules entry.",
            "First match wins: a nested copy shadows a hoisted one.",
            "That shadowing is how npm holds two versions in one tree."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Print The Chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "node -p \"require.resolve.paths('pkg')\"",
            "# every search dir, deepest first",
            "# NODE_DEBUG=module prints the misses too"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Splitting A Bare Specifier"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Specifier",
            "Package",
            "Subpath"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "lodash",
              "lodash",
              "."
            ],
            [
              "lodash/merge",
              "lodash",
              "./merge"
            ],
            [
              "@scope/pkg/sub",
              "@scope/pkg",
              "./sub"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scoped names eat two path segments, not one.",
            "`require('lodash/fp/get')` is plain file resolution inside the package.",
            "That deep import only works while `exports` does not block it.",
            "GLOBAL_FOLDERS ($HOME/.node_modules, $PREFIX/lib/node) searched last — legacy."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Legacy Search Roots",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NODE_PATH prepends extra search directories to the walk.",
            "Non-portable — your machine resolves, CI does not.",
            "Prefer workspaces or the `imports` field instead."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Symlink Realpath Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "By default Node resolves the realpath of a linked package.",
            "So `npm link` / pnpm store code uses its OWN node_modules chain.",
            "`--preserve-symlinks` keeps the link path instead.",
            "That flag is a classic source of duplicate-instance bugs."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Symlinks, Cache, Circular Requires",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Walk Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Item",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Worst case",
              "O(depth x candidates)"
            ],
            [
              "Unit",
              "failed stat() calls"
            ],
            [
              "Cached by",
              "specifier + parent"
            ],
            [
              "Paid",
              "once per unique pair"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deep nesting plus many bare imports = many misses at cold start.",
            "Real, measurable contributor to serverless cold-start time."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Install Strategies"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "npm: flat hoisting into the top node_modules.",
            "pnpm: symlinks into a content-addressed store.",
            "Same algorithm underneath — different tree shape.",
            "Hoisting causes phantom deps: importing what you never declared."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The CJS Wrapper"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "(function (exports, require, module,",
            "           __filename, __dirname) {",
            "  // your file's body lands here",
            "})"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Those five identifiers exist because they are parameters.",
            "`module.exports` is the real export value.",
            "`exports` is only an alias — `exports = {...}` exports nothing.",
            "Assign `module.exports = {...}` when replacing the whole object."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "require.cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keyed by resolved absolute filename.",
            "Second require of the same path returns the same object, no re-run.",
            "`delete require.cache[require.resolve('./x')]` forces a reload.",
            "Fine in tests, dangerous in prod — old references stay stale."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Identity is per path",
          "text": "The same package resolved at a hoisted path and a nested path yields two independent instances. That breaks singletons, `instanceof` checks, and React hooks."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Circular Requires"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// a.js",
            "exports.ready = false",
            "const b = require('./b')  // b sees ready=false",
            "exports.ready = true      // too late for b"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Symlinks, Cache, Circular Requires (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No throw: the partially filled module.exports is handed back.",
            "Late-defined properties read `undefined` at that instant.",
            "Fix: require lazily inside the function that needs it.",
            "Or export a function instead of destructured values."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Cycles Break Permanently"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`const { a } = require('./circular')` captures the snapshot.",
            "The later assignment never reaches your local `a`.",
            "ESM instead hoists and links bindings before evaluation.",
            "Function declarations survive a cycle; reading a `const` early throws TDZ."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "if (require.main === module) main()",
            "// classic 'am I the entry point' check",
            "console.log(module.parent) // null when entry"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Specifier Kinds",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Kind",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "relative",
              "'./x.js', '../y.js'"
            ],
            [
              "absolute URL",
              "'file:///abs/x.js', 'data:'"
            ],
            [
              "bare",
              "'lodash', '@scope/pkg/sub'"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Strictness Is The Point"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No extension guessing, no directory index fallback.",
            "'./util' throws ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND — write './util.js'.",
            "'./dir' throws too — write './dir/index.js'.",
            "Why: browser parity, no probing cost, unambiguous cache keys."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bare Specifiers In ESM"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same node_modules walk as CJS.",
            "Entry comes from `exports` first, then `main`, then legacy index."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Replacing __dirname"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'",
            "const f = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)",
            "const d = path.dirname(f)",
            "// Node 20.11+: import.meta.dirname"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`import.meta.url` is the ESM replacement for `__filename`.",
            "`import.meta.filename` / `.dirname` exist from Node 20.11.",
            "`import.meta.resolve(spec)` returns a URL string — the ESM require.resolve."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dynamic import()"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Accepts runtime strings; returns a Promise of the namespace.",
            "The only way to load ESM from CJS on older Node."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Import Attributes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "import d from './x.json' with { type: 'json' }",
            "// omit the attribute and Node throws",
            "// ERR_IMPORT_ATTRIBUTE_MISSING"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ESM Specifiers And The type Field",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cache Busting Costs Memory"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`await import('./m.js?t=' + Date.now())` reloads the module.",
            "The old instance leaks — there is no cache eviction API.",
            "Watch-mode reloaders pay this on every file save."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Allowed URL Schemes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Scheme",
            "State"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "file:",
              "supported"
            ],
            [
              "data:",
              "supported"
            ],
            [
              "node:",
              "supported"
            ],
            [
              "https:",
              "flag, experimental"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A real filename containing '#' or '?' must be percent-encoded.",
            "Unencoded, they parse as URL fragment and query."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "type Picks The Parser"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`type: commonjs` (also the default when absent): .js parses as CJS.",
            "`type: module`: .js parses as ESM.",
            "`.mjs` is ESM always; `.cjs` is CJS always — regardless of type.",
            "TypeScript mirrors this with `.mts` and `.cts`.",
            "The field is read from the NEAREST parent package.json, walking up."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flip One Subtree",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "// dist/cjs/package.json",
            "{ \"type\": \"commonjs\" }",
            "// only this folder becomes CJS"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Standard trick for a CJS build folder inside an ESM package.",
            "Format = extension + nearest package.json. Nothing else.",
            "How a file was imported never changes how it is parsed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Rule Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "File",
            "type field",
            "Format"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "a.js",
              "absent",
              "CJS"
            ],
            [
              "a.js",
              "module",
              "ESM"
            ],
            [
              "a.mjs",
              "any",
              "ESM"
            ],
            [
              "a.cjs",
              "any",
              "CJS"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Each Mode Forbids"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "type module: no require, no __dirname, no module.exports.",
            "type module: top-level `this` is undefined, not module.exports.",
            "type module: top-level await is allowed.",
            "CJS: no import/export syntax at all."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ESM Specifiers And The type Field (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two Signature Errors"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Error",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cannot use import statement",
              "file parsed as CJS"
            ],
            [
              "ERR_REQUIRE_ESM",
              "old Node requiring ESM"
            ],
            [
              "ERR_UNKNOWN_FILE_EXTENSION",
              "extensionless / odd ext"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "'Cannot use import statement outside a module' is the most-seen Node module error.",
            "ERR_REQUIRE_ESM only appears before require(esm) landed.",
            "Unknown extensions need a custom loader to work in ESM."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Breaking change",
          "text": "Adding `type: module` to a published package breaks consumers AND your own untouched .js files. Bump the major version."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "exports Replaces main"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The modern entry-point declaration, honoured by both resolvers.",
            "ESM from Node 12.7, CJS from 12.16.",
            "Keep `main` alongside it for old Node and older bundlers."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hard Encapsulation"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Once `exports` exists, ONLY listed subpaths are importable.",
            "`require('pkg/lib/internal.js')` throws ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED.",
            "The file still exists on disk — the resolver simply refuses."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sugar And Map Forms"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "\"exports\": \"./index.js\"",
            "\"exports\": {",
            "  \".\": \"./index.js\",",
            "  \"./utils\": \"./src/utils.js\",",
            "  \"./package.json\": \"./package.json\" }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A bare string is shorthand for the '.' entry.",
            "Always export ./package.json — many tools read it.",
            "All targets must be relative and start with './'.",
            "Bare or absolute targets throw ERR_INVALID_PACKAGE_TARGET."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Format Rules And The exports Field",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wildcard Subpaths",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "\"./features/*\": \"./src/features/*.js\",",
            "\"./features/internal/*\": null",
            "// 'pkg/features/x' -> src/features/x.js"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A single `*` is a non-greedy wildcard, used on both sides.",
            "A `null` target blocks a subpath — punch holes in a pattern.",
            "Most specific pattern wins: longest literal prefix."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Ordering Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Case",
            "Winner"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "conditions",
              "first matching key"
            ],
            [
              "patterns",
              "longest literal prefix"
            ],
            [
              "main vs exports",
              "exports, when present"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Trade-Off"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Gain: consumers cannot depend on internals, so you can refactor freely.",
            "Cost: you break the ecosystem habit of deep imports.",
            "So plan the public subpath list deliberately, up front.",
            "Non-goal: `exports` never restricts what the package loads internally."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Condition Maps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keys are condition names, values are targets or nested maps.",
            "Node picks the FIRST key it matches, in declaration order.",
            "`import` matches ESM resolution; `require` matches require().",
            "`node` matches any Node runtime.",
            "`default` always matches and MUST be last — later keys are dead."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Other Conditions"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Key",
            "Who sets it"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "node-addons",
              "native addon builds"
            ],
            [
              "browser",
              "community / bundlers"
            ],
            [
              "development",
              "--conditions"
            ],
            [
              "production",
              "--conditions"
            ],
            [
              "types",
              "TypeScript, first"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Custom Conditions"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "node --conditions=my-cond app.js",
            "node -C my-cond app.js   # alias",
            "# ships a special build per runtime"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Canonical Dual Entry"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "\".\": {",
            "  \"types\": \"./index.d.ts\",",
            "  \"import\": \"./esm/index.mjs\",",
            "  \"require\": \"./cjs/index.cjs\",",
            "  \"default\": \"./esm/index.mjs\" }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Subpath Patterns And Conditions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Conditions and subpaths nest in either order.",
            "Subpath map holding condition maps, or the reverse — both legal.",
            "An array target is a fallback list: first valid entry wins.",
            "Arrays are rarely needed and badly supported by old tools."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "types Goes First",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "TypeScript also does first-match-wins on condition keys.",
            "Put `types` before `import` and `require` or it is never reached.",
            "`module` and `jsnext:main` are bundler folklore — Node ignores them."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Which Branch Won?"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "node --conditions=x -e \\",
            "  \"console.log(import.meta.resolve('pkg'))\"",
            "# or require.resolve('pkg') for the CJS side"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Key Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// require('pkg') on Node, map above",
            "// tries: types, import, require",
            "// 'require' hits: ./cjs/index.cjs",
            "// import 'pkg' would stop at 'import'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same map, two entry files — one declaration order decides both.",
            "Move `default` up and everything below it dies silently."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ship A Test-Only Build"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "\".\": { \"test\": \"./src/mock.js\",",
            "       \"default\": \"./dist/real.js\" }",
            "// run it: node -C test suite.js"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Mock adapters swap in at resolution time — no bundler alias.",
            "Same lever drives development / production splits."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Subpath Patterns And Conditions (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Exports Error Codes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "PATH_NOT_EXPORTED",
              "deep import blocked"
            ],
            [
              "INVALID_PACKAGE_TARGET",
              "bare or absolute target"
            ],
            [
              "target missing",
              "files field dropped it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Check Before Publish"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Checks"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "publint",
              "exports targets"
            ],
            [
              "arethetypeswrong",
              "types per mode"
            ],
            [
              "npm pack",
              "files actually shipped"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Most condition-map bugs are caught statically, before publish.",
            "Smoke test both: require('pkg') and import('pkg') same shape."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The imports Field"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "\"imports\": {",
            "  \"#db\": { \"node\": \"./src/db-pg.js\",",
            "           \"default\": \"./src/db-memory.js\" },",
            "  \"#internal/*\": \"./src/internal/*.js\" }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every key MUST start with '#'.",
            "That is exactly why '#' can never be a node_modules package name.",
            "Inside the package: `import db from '#db'`.",
            "Patterns kill the '../../../src/internal/x.js' pyramid — no build step."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Private By Construction"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only resolvable from inside the declaring package.",
            "Your consumers cannot import '#db' from your package.",
            "Targets may be relative files OR bare specifiers.",
            "So `\"#lodash\": \"lodash-es\"` is legal — `exports` forbids that."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Every 'Cannot use import statement outside a module' you have ever hit comes from one of three decisions Node makes before your code runs: which parser, which path, which copy. This handbook walks the actual CJS probing order and the ESM URL rules, then the package.json fields — type, exports, imports — that steer both. Ends with the dual-package hazard and the debug commands that print exactly what won.",
